{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "id": "structure-residue-templates",
 "title": "Standard-residue heavy-atom connectivity templates",
 "notes": [
  "A PDB or mmCIF coordinate file CARRIES NO BOND GRAPH. ATOM records are positions and names;",
  "CONECT is optional, is only ever written for non-standard groups, and is absent from most",
  "entries. So bonds for standard residues have to come from somewhere, and this pack is that",
  "somewhere: the connectivity of each standard residue by ATOM NAME, which the file does give.",
  "Heavy atoms only. Hydrogens are absent from most crystal structures and are not needed by the",
  "cartoon or stick renderer, so adding them here would create bonds to atoms that are not there.",
  "Bond orders are chemical facts about the residue, not measurements of this structure. Aromatic",
  "rings are marked 'ar' rather than being Kekule-alternated, because the alternation is a",
  "drawing convention and picking one would assert a tautomer the file does not state.",
  "OXT and OP3 appear only on terminal residues; a template bond whose atom is absent is simply",
  "not created and is counted in the diagnostics, never guessed at.",
  "An UNRECOGNISED residue name is REPORTED (name and count) and left unbonded. It is never",
  "bonded by a distance guess dressed up as a template - a distance guess is a different claim",
  "and lives behind ConnectivityOptions::inferByDistance, off by default, and every bond it",
  "makes is marked inferred."
 ],
